{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EoQAwZy3LonN6ho3z2sffk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Deterministic consolidation job for \"detect duplicate memories\".\n2\t//!\n3\t//! This implements the `## 6. Consolidation Engine` consolidation-jobs bullet\n4\t//! \"detect duplicate memories\" from\n5\t//! `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md`.\n6\t\n7\tuse std::collections::{BTreeMap, BTreeSet};\n8\tuse std::time::Instant;\n9\t\n10\tuse serde_json::json;\n11\tuse tracing::info_span;\n12\t\n13\tuse super::{\n14\t    capture_memory_state, encode_memory_state, ConsolidationJobMode, ConsolidationJobRuntime,\n15\t    PendingProposalSpec, ProposalKind, ScanError, ScanReport,\n16\t};\n17\tuse crate::embeddings::{cosine_similarity, fingerprint_text};\n18\tuse crate::memory::{Memory, MemoryStore};\n19\tuse crate::storage::VectorStore;\n20\t\n21\tconst DEFAULT_DUPLICATE_THRESHOLD: f32 = 0.92;\n22\tconst TOP_K_NEIGHBORS: usize = 6;\n23\t\n24\tpub struct DuplicateDetector<'a> {\n25\t    store: &'a MemoryStore,\n26\t    runtime: &'a mut ConsolidationJobRuntime,\n27\t    threshold: f32,\n28\t}\n29\t\n30\timpl<'a> DuplicateDetector<'a> {\n31\t    pub fn new(store: &'a MemoryStore, runtime: &'a mut ConsolidationJobRuntime) -> Self {\n32\t        Self {\n33\t            store,\n34\t            runtime,\n35\t            threshold: DEFAULT_DUPLICATE_THRESHOLD,\n36\t        }\n37\t    }\n38\t\n39\t    pub fn with_threshold(mut self, threshold: f32) -> Self {\n40\t        self.threshold = threshold;\n41\t        self\n42\t    }\n43\t\n44\t    pub fn scan(\n45\t        &mut self,\n46\t        workspace_id: &str,\n47\t        kind_filter: Option<ProposalKind>,\n48\t    ) -> Result<ScanReport, ScanError> {\n49\t        let started = Instant::now();\n50\t        let span = info_span!(\n51\t            \"consolidation.duplicates.scan\",\n52\t            workspace_id,\n53\t            kind = \"detect duplicate memories\"\n54\t        );\n55\t        let _entered = span.enter();\n56\t        let memories = self.store.list_workspace_memories(workspace_id)?;\n57\t        if memories.is_empty() {\n58\t            return Ok(ScanReport::from_counts(0, 0, started));\n59\t        }\n60\t\n61\t        let mut proposals_enqueued = 0u32;\n62\t        let mut skipped = 0u32;\n63\t        let mut seen_pairs = BTreeSet::new();\n64\t\n65\t        for bucket in bucket_memories(&memories).into_values() {\n66\t            let index = build_index(&bucket)?;\n67\t            for memory in &bucket {\n68\t                let query = fingerprint_text(&memory.content);\n69\t                let neighbors = index\n70\t                    .search(&query, TOP_K_NEIGHBORS)\n71\t                    .map_err(ScanError::from)?;\n72\t                for (_, neighbor_id, _, _) in neighbors {\n73\t                    if memory.id == neighbor_id {\n74\t                        continue;\n75\t                    }\n76\t                    let Some(candidate) = bucket.iter().find(|entry| entry.id == neighbor_id)\n77\t                    else {\n78\t                        continue;\n79\t                    };\n80\t                    let pair_key = ordered_pair(&memory.id, &candidate.id);\n81\t                    if !seen_pairs.insert(pair_key) {\n82\t                        continue;\n83\t                    }\n84\t                    if !shares_typed_evidence(memory, candidate) {\n85\t                        skipped += 1;\n86\t                        continue;\n87\t                    }\n88\t                    let similarity =\n89\t                        cosine_similarity(&query, &fingerprint_text(&candidate.content));\n90\t                    if similarity < self.threshold {\n91\t                        skipped += 1;\n92\t                        continue;\n93\t                    }\n94\t\n95\t                    let older = older_memory(memory, candidate);\n96\t                    let newer = newer_memory(memory, candidate);\n97\t                    let both_stale = older.is_stale && newer.is_stale;\n98\t                    let proposal_kind = if both_stale {\n99\t                        ProposalKind::Demote\n100\t                    } else {\n101\t                        ProposalKind::Supersede\n102\t                    };\n103\t                    if kind_filter.is_some() && kind_filter != Some(proposal_kind) {\n104\t                        skipped += 1;\n105\t                        continue;\n106\t                    }\n107\t\n108\t                    let prior_state = capture_memory_state(self.store, older)?;\n109\t                    let proposed_state = if proposal_kind == ProposalKind::Demote {\n110\t                        let mut next = prior_state.clone();\n111\t                        next.memory.confidence = (next.memory.confidence - 0.15).max(0.1);\n112\t                        if next.structured_fields.verification_status\n113\t                            == crate::memory::MemoryVerificationStatus::Verified\n114\t                        {\n115\t                            next.structured_fields.verification_status =\n116\t                                crate::memory::MemoryVerificationStatus::Unverified;\n117\t                        }\n118\t                        next\n119\t                    } else {\n120\t                        let mut next = prior_state.clone();\n121\t                        next.structured_fields.verification_status =\n122\t                            crate::memory::MemoryVerificationStatus::Superseded;\n123\t                        next.structured_fields.superseded_by_memory_id = Some(newer.id.clone());\n124\t                        next.memory_links.push(crate::memory::MemoryLinkRecord {\n125\t                            link_id: format!(\"dup:{}:{}\", older.id, newer.id),\n126\t                            source_memory_id: older.id.clone(),\n127\t                            target_memory_id: newer.id.clone(),\n128\t                            link_type: \"supersedes\".to_string(),\n129\t                            reason: \"duplicate detector matched overlapping evidence\".to_string(),\n130\t                            created_at: newer.created_at,\n131\t                            verification_status: \"verified\".to_string(),\n132\t                        });\n133\t                        next\n134\t                    };\n135\t\n136\t                    enqueue(\n137\t                        self.runtime,\n138\t                        workspace_id,\n139\t                        format!(\"duplicate-detection-{}-{}\", older.id, newer.id),\n140\t                        PendingProposalSpec {\n141\t                            proposal_id: format!(\"duplicate-proposal-{}-{}\", older.id, newer.id),\n142\t                            target_memory_id: Some(older.id.clone()),\n143\t                            proposal_kind,\n144\t                            prior_state: encode_memory_state(&prior_state),\n145\t                            proposed_state: encode_memory_state(&proposed_state),\n146\t                            evidence: json!({\n147\t                                \"source_memory_ids\": [older.id.clone(), newer.id.clone()],\n148\t                                \"similarity\": similarity,\n149\t                                \"shared_files\": shared_values(&older.linked_files, &newer.linked_files),\n150\t                                \"shared_symbols\": shared_values(&older.linked_symbols, &newer.linked_symbols),\n151\t                            }),\n152\t                            provenance: None,\n153\t                        },\n154\t                    )?;\n155\t                    proposals_enqueued += 1;\n156\t                }\n157\t            }\n158\t        }\n159\t\n160\t        let _ = self.runtime.run_due()?;\n161\t        Ok(ScanReport::from_counts(\n162\t            proposals_enqueued,\n163\t            skipped,\n164\t            started,\n165\t        ))\n166\t    }\n167\t}\n168\t\n169\tfn bucket_memories(memories: &[Memory]) -> BTreeMap<(String, String), Vec<Memory>> {\n170\t    let mut buckets = BTreeMap::new();\n171\t    for memory in memories {\n172\t        buckets\n173\t            .entry((\n174\t                memory.memory_type.as_str().to_string(),\n175\t                memory.scope.as_str().to_string(),\n176\t            ))\n177\t            .or_insert_with(Vec::new)\n178\t            .push(memory.clone());\n179\t    }\n180\t    buckets\n181\t}\n182\t\n183\tfn build_index(memories: &[Memory]) -> Result<VectorStore, ScanError> {\n184\t    let index = VectorStore::open_in_memory()?;\n185\t    index.initialize(64)?;\n186\t    for memory in memories {\n187\t        let vector = fingerprint_text(&memory.content);\n188\t        index.upsert_vector(&memory.id, \"memory\", 0, &vector)?;\n189\t    }\n190\t    Ok(index)\n191\t}\n192\t\n193\tfn ordered_pair(left: &str, right: &str) -> (String, String) {\n194\t    if left <= right {\n195\t        (left.to_string(), right.to_string())\n196\t    } else {\n197\t        (right.to_string(), left.to_string())\n198\t    }\n199\t}\n200\t\n201\tfn older_memory<'a>(left: &'a Memory, right: &'a Memory) -> &'a Memory {\n202\t    if left.created_at <= right.created_at {\n203\t        left\n204\t    } else {\n205\t        right\n206\t    }\n207\t}\n208\t\n209\tfn newer_memory<'a>(left: &'a Memory, right: &'a Memory) -> &'a Memory {\n210\t    if left.created_at >= right.created_at {\n211\t        left\n212\t    } else {\n213\t        right\n214\t    }\n215\t}\n216\t\n217\tfn shares_typed_evidence(left: &Memory, right: &Memory) -> bool {\n218\t    !shared_values(&left.linked_files, &right.linked_files).is_empty()\n219\t        || !shared_values(&left.linked_symbols, &right.linked_symbols).is_empty()\n220\t}\n221\t\n222\tfn shared_values(left: &[String], right: &[String]) -> Vec<String> {\n223\t    let right_values = right.iter().collect::<BTreeSet<_>>();\n224\t    left.iter()\n225\t        .filter(|value| right_values.contains(value))\n226\t        .cloned()\n227\t        .collect()\n228\t}\n229\t\n230\tfn enqueue(\n231\t    runtime: &mut ConsolidationJobRuntime,\n232\t    workspace_id: &str,\n233\t    job_id: String,\n234\t    proposal: PendingProposalSpec,\n235\t) -> Result<(), ScanError> {\n236\t    runtime\n237\t        .submit(crate::consolidation::ConsolidationJobSpec {\n238\t            job_id,\n239\t            workspace_id: workspace_id.to_string(),\n240\t            kind: \"detect duplicate memories\".to_string(),\n241\t            mode: ConsolidationJobMode::Background,\n242\t            proposal: Some(proposal),\n243\t        })\n244\t        .map_err(ScanError::from)\n245\t        .map(|_| ())\n246\t}\n247\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67f9c4ff-29cf-4b48-8541-b2a63bf25834","uuid":"82b818cf-2edc-4baf-b5b7-a4fb888f76c2","timestamp":"2026-05-17T11:39:34.356Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/duplicates.rs","content":"//! Deterministic consolidation job for \"detect duplicate memories\".\n//!\n//! This implements the `## 6. Consolidation Engine` consolidation-jobs bullet\n//! \"detect duplicate memories\" from\n//! `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md`.\n\nuse std::collections::{BTreeMap, BTreeSet};\nuse std::time::Instant;\n\nuse serde_json::json;\nuse tracing::info_span;\n\nuse super::{\n    capture_memory_state, encode_memory_state, ConsolidationJobMode, ConsolidationJobRuntime,\n    PendingProposalSpec, ProposalKind, ScanError, ScanReport,\n};\nuse crate::embeddings::{cosine_similarity, fingerprint_text};\nuse crate::memory::{Memory, MemoryStore};\nuse crate::storage::VectorStore;\n\nconst DEFAULT_DUPLICATE_THRESHOLD: f32 = 0.92;\nconst TOP_K_NEIGHBORS: usize = 6;\n\npub struct DuplicateDetector<'a> {\n    store: &'a MemoryStore,\n    runtime: &'a mut ConsolidationJobRuntime,\n    threshold: f32,\n}\n\nimpl<'a> DuplicateDetector<'a> {\n    pub fn new(store: &'a MemoryStore, runtime: &'a mut ConsolidationJobRuntime) -> Self {\n        Self {\n            store,\n            runtime,\n            threshold: DEFAULT_DUPLICATE_THRESHOLD,\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub fn with_threshold(mut self, threshold: f32) -> Self {\n        self.threshold = threshold;\n        self\n    }\n\n    pub fn scan(\n        &mut self,\n        workspace_id: &str,\n        kind_filter: Option<ProposalKind>,\n    ) -> Result<ScanReport, ScanError> {\n        let started = Instant::now();\n        let span = info_span!(\n            \"consolidation.duplicates.scan\",\n            workspace_id,\n            kind = \"detect duplicate memories\"\n        );\n        let _entered = span.enter();\n        let memories = self.store.list_workspace_memories(workspace_id)?;\n        if memories.is_empty() {\n            return Ok(ScanReport::from_counts(0, 0, started));\n        }\n\n        let mut proposals_enqueued = 0u32;\n        let mut skipped = 0u32;\n        let mut seen_pairs = BTreeSet::new();\n\n        for bucket in bucket_memories(&memories).into_values() {\n            let index = build_index(&bucket)?;\n            for memory in &bucket {\n                let query = fingerprint_text(&memory.content);\n                let neighbors = index\n                    .search(&query, TOP_K_NEIGHBORS)\n                    .map_err(ScanError::from)?;\n                for (_, neighbor_id, _, _) in neighbors {\n                    if memory.id == neighbor_id {\n                        continue;\n                    }\n                    let Some(candidate) = bucket.iter().find(|entry| entry.id == neighbor_id)\n                    else {\n                        continue;\n                    };\n                    let pair_key = ordered_pair(&memory.id, &candidate.id);\n                    if !seen_pairs.insert(pair_key) {\n                        continue;\n                    }\n                    if !shares_typed_evidence(memory, candidate) {\n                        skipped += 1;\n                        continue;\n                    }\n                    let similarity =\n                        cosine_similarity(&query, &fingerprint_text(&candidate.content));\n                    if similarity < self.threshold {\n                        skipped += 1;\n                        continue;\n                    }\n\n                    let older = older_memory(memory, candidate);\n                    let newer = newer_memory(memory, candidate);\n                    let both_stale = older.is_stale && newer.is_stale;\n                    let proposal_kind = if both_stale {\n                        ProposalKind::Demote\n                    } else {\n                        ProposalKind::Supersede\n                    };\n                    if kind_filter.is_some() && kind_filter != Some(proposal_kind) {\n                        skipped += 1;\n                        continue;\n                    }\n\n                    let prior_state = capture_memory_state(self.store, older)?;\n                    let proposed_state = if proposal_kind == ProposalKind::Demote {\n                        let mut next = prior_state.clone();\n                        next.memory.confidence = (next.memory.confidence - 0.15).max(0.1);\n                        if next.structured_fields.verification_status\n                            == crate::memory::MemoryVerificationStatus::Verified\n                        {\n                            next.structured_fields.verification_status =\n                                crate::memory::MemoryVerificationStatus::Unverified;\n                        }\n                        next\n                    } else {\n                        let mut next = prior_state.clone();\n                        next.structured_fields.verification_status =\n                            crate::memory::MemoryVerificationStatus::Superseded;\n                        next.structured_fields.superseded_by_memory_id = Some(newer.id.clone());\n                        next.memory_links.push(crate::memory::MemoryLinkRecord {\n                            link_id: format!(\"dup:{}:{}\", older.id, newer.id),\n                            source_memory_id: older.id.clone(),\n                            target_memory_id: newer.id.clone(),\n                            link_type: \"supersedes\".to_string(),\n                            reason: \"duplicate detector matched overlapping evidence\".to_string(),\n                            created_at: newer.created_at,\n                            verification_status: \"verified\".to_string(),\n                        });\n                        next\n                    };\n\n                    enqueue(\n                        self.runtime,\n                        workspace_id,\n                        format!(\"duplicate-detection-{}-{}\", older.id, newer.id),\n                        PendingProposalSpec {\n                            proposal_id: format!(\"duplicate-proposal-{}-{}\", older.id, newer.id),\n                            target_memory_id: Some(older.id.clone()),\n                            proposal_kind,\n                            prior_state: encode_memory_state(&prior_state),\n                            proposed_state: encode_memory_state(&proposed_state),\n                            evidence: json!({\n                                \"source_memory_ids\": [older.id.clone(), newer.id.clone()],\n                                \"similarity\": similarity,\n                                \"shared_files\": shared_values(&older.linked_files, &newer.linked_files),\n                                \"shared_symbols\": shared_values(&older.linked_symbols, &newer.linked_symbols),\n                            }),\n                            provenance: None,\n                        },\n                    )?;\n                    proposals_enqueued += 1;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        let _ = self.runtime.run_due()?;\n        Ok(ScanReport::from_counts(\n            proposals_enqueued,\n            skipped,\n            started,\n        ))\n    }\n}\n\nfn bucket_memories(memories: &[Memory]) -> BTreeMap<(String, String), Vec<Memory>> {\n    let mut buckets = BTreeMap::new();\n    for memory in memories {\n        buckets\n            .entry((\n                memory.memory_type.as_str().to_string(),\n                memory.scope.as_str().to_string(),\n            ))\n            .or_insert_with(Vec::new)\n            .push(memory.clone());\n    }\n    buckets\n}\n\nfn build_index(memories: &[Memory]) -> Result<VectorStore, ScanError> {\n    let index = VectorStore::open_in_memory()?;\n    index.initialize(64)?;\n    for memory in memories {\n        let vector = fingerprint_text(&memory.content);\n        index.upsert_vector(&memory.id, \"memory\", 0, &vector)?;\n    }\n    Ok(index)\n}\n\nfn ordered_pair(left: &str, right: &str) -> (String, String) {\n    if left <= right {\n        (left.to_string(), right.to_string())\n    } else {\n        (right.to_string(), left.to_string())\n    }\n}\n\nfn older_memory<'a>(left: &'a Memory, right: &'a Memory) -> &'a Memory {\n    if left.created_at <= right.created_at {\n        left\n    } else {\n        right\n    }\n}\n\nfn newer_memory<'a>(left: &'a Memory, right: &'a Memory) -> &'a Memory {\n    if left.created_at >= right.created_at {\n        left\n    } else {\n        right\n    }\n}\n\nfn shares_typed_evidence(left: &Memory, right: &Memory) -> bool {\n    !shared_values(&left.linked_files, &right.linked_files).is_empty()\n        || !shared_values(&left.linked_symbols, &right.linked_symbols).is_empty()\n}\n\nfn shared_values(left: &[String], right: &[String]) -> Vec<String> {\n    let right_values = right.iter().collect::<BTreeSet<_>>();\n    left.iter()\n        .filter(|value| right_values.contains(value))\n        .cloned()\n        .collect()\n}\n\nfn enqueue(\n    runtime: &mut ConsolidationJobRuntime,\n    workspace_id: &str,\n    job_id: String,\n    proposal: PendingProposalSpec,\n) -> Result<(), ScanError> {\n    runtime\n        .submit(crate::consolidation::ConsolidationJobSpec {\n            job_id,\n            workspace_id: workspace_id.to_string(),\n            kind: \"detect duplicate memories\".to_string(),\n            mode: ConsolidationJobMode::Background,\n            proposal: Some(proposal),\n        })\n        .map_err(ScanError::from)\n        .map(|_| ())\n}\n","numLines":247,"startLine":1,"totalLines":247}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01MgmLm47iBiBsmXSMGB78T9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011L8L1RKdnwYgqqJihYRwJK","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-llm-budgets.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5127,"cache_read_input_tokens":85624,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5127},"output_tokens":57,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67f9c4ff-29cf-4b48-8541-b2a63bf25834","uuid":"6bb8d65b-86de-4cd1-9b47-b0e299f7f6c3","request_id":"req_011Cb85Q2gL6Q9F4KUBN3muH"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011L8L1RKdnwYgqqJihYRwJK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Consolidation LLM Budgets\n2\t\n3\t## Scope\n4\t\n5\tThis note defines the default budget, bounded queue, failure, and provenance contract for Phase 6 LLM-driven consolidation jobs: episode summary generation, procedure extraction, contradiction detection, and failure-pattern extraction. `BudgetCatalog` in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/llm/budget.rs` is the canonical source of truth; this document mirrors those defaults for operators.\n6\t\n7\t## Per-job budgets\n8\t\n9\t| job_kind | max_prompt_tokens | max_response_tokens | max_latency_ms | max_cost_micro_usd | fallback_strategy |\n10\t|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\n11\t| episode_summary | 6000 | 1200 | 8000 | 250 | deterministic episode template |\n12\t| procedure_extraction | 10000 | 1800 | 12000 | 450 | skip and mark affected memory stale |\n13\t| contradiction_detection | 3000 | 800 | 5000 | 125 | deterministic supersession candidate |\n14\t| failure_pattern_extraction | 7000 | 1400 | 9000 | 300 | skip and mark affected memory stale |\n15\t\n16\t## Bounded queue depth\n17\t\n18\tThe consolidation queue is globally bounded by `ConsolidationConfig::max_queue_depth`. LLM submission can additionally use a per-kind slice quota through `BoundedJobQueue::with_per_kind_max_depth`. When a slice is full, the daemon drops the incoming job, persists it as `dropped`, emits a `tracing::warn!` with `workspace_id`, `kind`, `current_depth`, and `max_depth`, and writes a `ConsolidationFailed` event with `error_kind = \"queue_full\"`.\n19\t\n20\t## Failure handling\n21\t\n22\tMalformed responses, driver failures, budget overruns, and queue-full drops leave prior memory state unchanged. The failure path emits `ConsolidationFailed` before returning, with the job id, job kind, mode, model name, error kind, and actionable error message. Budget overruns either use the documented deterministic fallback strategy or skip with a stale flag rather than accepting an over-budget LLM response.\n23\t\n24\t## Provenance record\n25\t\n26\tEvery successful LLM proposal stores `provenance_json` on `consolidation_proposals`. The record contains `model`, `prompt_sha256`, `response_sha256`, `prompt_token_count`, `response_token_count`, `latency_ms`, and `called_at`. Hashes use SHA-256 over the exact prompt and response bytes, which lets operators verify that a proposal came from the recorded prompt and response without storing either blob in the proposal row.\n27\t\n28\t## Operator overrides\n29\t\n30\tOperators override budgets by constructing `ConsolidationConfig` with `llm_budget_catalog: Some(BudgetCatalog { ... })`; otherwise `BudgetCatalog::default()` supplies the pinned values above. Queue depth is controlled by `max_queue_depth`, and LLM per-kind slice depth is configured on `BoundedJobQueue` where the LLM submission surface owns the event writer required for queue-full audit events.\n31\t\n32\t## Spec citation\n33\t\n34\tThis contract implements [§6. Consolidation Engine](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#6-consolidation-engine), specifically the \"LLM-driven consolidation\" bullets requiring model/prompt/response provenance, bounded queue drops with warnings, and documented cost and latency budgets with deterministic fallback or stale marking.\n35\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67f9c4ff-29cf-4b48-8541-b2a63bf25834","uuid":"e131c575-5475-4fd7-a8a8-abf7e3176321","timestamp":"2026-05-17T11:39:35.082Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-llm-budgets.md","content":"# Consolidation LLM Budgets\n\n## Scope\n\nThis note defines the default budget, bounded queue, failure, and provenance contract for Phase 6 LLM-driven consolidation jobs: episode summary generation, procedure extraction, contradiction detection, and failure-pattern extraction. `BudgetCatalog` in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/llm/budget.rs` is the canonical source of truth; this document mirrors those defaults for operators.\n\n## Per-job budgets\n\n| job_kind | max_prompt_tokens | max_response_tokens | max_latency_ms | max_cost_micro_usd | fallback_strategy |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| episode_summary | 6000 | 1200 | 8000 | 250 | deterministic episode template |\n| procedure_extraction | 10000 | 1800 | 12000 | 450 | skip and mark affected memory stale |\n| contradiction_detection | 3000 | 800 | 5000 | 125 | deterministic supersession candidate |\n| failure_pattern_extraction | 7000 | 1400 | 9000 | 300 | skip and mark affected memory stale |\n\n## Bounded queue depth\n\nThe consolidation queue is globally bounded by `ConsolidationConfig::max_queue_depth`. LLM submission can additionally use a per-kind slice quota through `BoundedJobQueue::with_per_kind_max_depth`. When a slice is full, the daemon drops the incoming job, persists it as `dropped`, emits a `tracing::warn!` with `workspace_id`, `kind`, `current_depth`, and `max_depth`, and writes a `ConsolidationFailed` event with `error_kind = \"queue_full\"`.\n\n## Failure handling\n\nMalformed responses, driver failures, budget overruns, and queue-full drops leave prior memory state unchanged. The failure path emits `ConsolidationFailed` before returning, with the job id, job kind, mode, model name, error kind, and actionable error message. Budget overruns either use the documented deterministic fallback strategy or skip with a stale flag rather than accepting an over-budget LLM response.\n\n## Provenance record\n\nEvery successful LLM proposal stores `provenance_json` on `consolidation_proposals`. The record contains `model`, `prompt_sha256`, `response_sha256`, `prompt_token_count`, `response_token_count`, `latency_ms`, and `called_at`. Hashes use SHA-256 over the exact prompt and response bytes, which lets operators verify that a proposal came from the recorded prompt and response without storing either blob in the proposal row.\n\n## Operator overrides\n\nOperators override budgets by constructing `ConsolidationConfig` with `llm_budget_catalog: Some(BudgetCatalog { ... })`; otherwise `BudgetCatalog::default()` supplies the pinned values above. Queue depth is controlled by `max_queue_depth`, and LLM per-kind slice depth is configured on `BoundedJobQueue` where the LLM submission surface owns the event writer required for queue-full audit events.\n\n## Spec citation\n\nThis contract implements [§6. Consolidation Engine](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#6-consolidation-engine), specifically the \"LLM-driven consolidation\" bullets requiring model/prompt/response provenance, bounded queue drops with warnings, and documented cost and latency budgets with deterministic fallback or stale marking.\n","numLines":35,"startLine":1,"totalLines":35}}}
